<ul>
<li>
<p>Left pointer: The left pointer will always point to a value less than or=
 equal to the value at the right pointer because the array is sorted. Incre=
menting it would result in a sum greater than or equal to the current sum o=
f 1.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Right pointer: Decrementing the right pointer would result in a sum that=
=E2=80=99s less than or equal to 1.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Therefore, we should increment the left pointer to find a larger sum:</p=
